course: dictionary
lesson: 10513
title: Twisty: bends in roads and turns in stories
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Twisty is a describing word. It tells you that something is full of twists and bends. «The path up the hill was twisty, so we could not see the top.» The path bends again and again, so twisty means winding and bendy. Check it by putting your meaning in the sentence and reading it again.
explain: Twisty can also describe a story. A twisty plot has many surprising turns, so you cannot guess the ending. A twisty road and a twisty plot both have turns, but one is on the ground and one is in the story.
explain: Look at the words around twisty to see what it describes. «Crack an egg into a glass bowl and you can count its parts: the yellow yolk, the clear white, and two twisty white cords that hold the yolk in the middle.» The cords are not straight. They wind, so they must be twisty in shape.
fact: Twisty means full of twists and bends.
fact: «A twisty road» is a road with lots of bends.
fact: A «twisty plot» is a story with many surprising turns.
fact: Twistier means more twisty, and twistiest means the most twisty.
fact: In an egg, the two «twisty white cords» hold the yolk in the middle, like the ropes of a hammock.
exercise: «The twisty path wound between the trees.» What does twisty mean here? | *Full of bends and turns | Covered in snow | Very wide | Straight and flat
exercise: The book had a twisty plot. What does twisty mean for a story? | It is about twisting ropes | *It has many surprising turns | It has no words | It is very short
exercise: Which word means the most twisty? | twist | twistier | *twistiest | twisty
test: «Two twisty white cords hold the yolk in the middle.» What do the cords look like? | Straight and stiff | *Winding, like twisted ropes | Round like a ball | Clear and runny
test: Ella says a twisty road is a flat, straight road. What does twisty really mean? | Flat and smooth | Very short and narrow | Straight, with no corners | *Full of bends and turns
exam: Which sentence uses twisty correctly? | She twisty ate her soup | The cake was twisty and sweet | *The mountain road was twisty, with a bend every few metres | The sky was twisty and blue
